{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "All's Well That Ends Well", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Nothing Ventured ...", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "get something off your chest ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say something you have wanted to say for a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have to get something off my chest.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you are eavesdropping.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I'm not that guy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I don't normally behave that way or have those mannerisms", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not that guy. I'm not the possessive type.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals to Express Annoyance in the Present and in the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals in their present and past forms to express annoyance about a situation or to make a critical comment.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to express annoyance and criticism about the past, you can use modals such as  <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">could</span></span>, <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">might</span></span>, <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">should</span></span>, <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">ought to</span></span>, and <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">would + have + the past participle of the verb</span></span>. This structure adds meaning to the main verb and can convey annoyance when you use them properly.<br/> Remember, when you talk about annoyance in the past, you use the <span class = \"strong\">modal + have + past participle</span>. Take a look at the chart below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Peter, you <span class=\"strong\">can</span> be so insensitive!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">could</span> at least think about my feelings once. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> go now? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You  <span class=\"strong\">might</span> let me know the next time you are going to save the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\"> might have</span> let me know before we started dating that you were really just a child.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\"> could have</span> told me about that guy in New York!", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Could</span> you put the toilet seat down after using it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can/would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to express annoyance\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> be a little needy. <br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Would</span> that be asking too much?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"could/might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to express annoyance when someone doesn't do something \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might</span> let me know when she's going to fly to Africa for a week!<br/>You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> at least think about my feelings once.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"could have/<br/>might have/<br/>would have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to make a critical comment\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have</span> told me about that guy in New York!<br/> He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might have</span> offered to pay.<br/> You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have</span> told me about the changes in the report!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Notice that the meaning of those expressions depend on the right context and tone of voice.<br/><br/> For example: <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I took Carol out to dinner last night, because it was her birthday. I didn't tell her I got fired one week ago. She <span class=\"strong\">might have</span> offered to pay.</span><br/><br/>  In this sentence, the speaker does not express annoyance; he is expressing a possibility.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Willingness and Intention", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Will</span> and <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> are modals. You can use these modals to express willingness and intention. Willingness can be defined as the readiness to do something. Intention can be defined as an aim or plan.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">will</span> to express willingness in the present. </br></br> For example:<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\">  Richard is a nice person. He <span class=\"strong\">will</span> always help if you need something. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use will in the first person, it can express intention.</br></br>  For example: </br></br><span class=\"italic\"> I'<span class=\"strong\">ll </span>do my homework later tonight.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> to express willingness in the past. </br></br> For example: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\">My father was a kind person. He <span class=\"strong\">would</span> always help you if you were in trouble.</span></br></br>  Take a look at some examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'll</span>  give you my office if you need it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'll</span>  do anything to make you happy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">will</span>  take you to the office. It is raining.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My boss <span class=\"strong\">won't</span>  let me go earlier.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I talked to the manager at the shop, but they <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span>  give a discount.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "needy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wanting too much attention and love", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I can be a little needy and a little insecure and I was both yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pang", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a \u200bsudden \u200bsharp \u200bfeeling, \u200bespecially of \u200bpainful \u200bemotion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I felt this wild pang of fear.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to eavesdrop", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to listen to a conversation secretly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was eavesdropping on their conversation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss with my partner the last time I had an argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I collaborate with my partner to create a fake argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express annoyance in the present and the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present it to the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss with a partner the last time you had an argument with someone. What was it about? Where was it?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, pretend someone is listening and create a fake argument about a situation of your choosing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Express annoyance and anger about your partner's present and past activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make the conversation as outlandish as you wish.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present it to the class.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le16ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le16ob09re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le16ob09re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob09re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Hi, Amy.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Hi, Vanessa. Could I have a word with Peter alone?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sure. I'll give you my office. Peter knows where it is.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'll start. I have to get something off my chest. I am so sorry for the way I acted yesterday. I have no right to make demands of you or to have any expectations of you. I'm not that guy. I'm not the possessive type who has to keep tabs on your every movement. Unfortunately, I can be a little needy and a little insecure and I was both yesterday. The truth is, you are the best thing that has ever happened to me and I felt this wild pang of fear that this trip might be the beginning of the end for us. I like us. I want us to keep going. I'll do anything. I'll wash clothes, I'll cook dinner. Would you be willing to give me another chance?", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob09re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Thank you for saying that Peter. That means a lot to me. I might have been angrier, but deep down I knew that you were coming from a place of love.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I would have apologized earlier, but I didn't know what to say.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Let me also say, that I could have been a little more sensitive toward your feelings as well.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Will you give me a hug?</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Amy. Look.  Someone is listening in.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: You want to give them a show?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yeah!\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Peter you can be so crass!", "id": 2, "time": "60000"}, {"image": "engenn11le16ob09re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You could at least think about my feelings once. Do you have to go now? You might let me know the next time you are going to save the world.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: You might have let me know before we started dating that you were really just a child.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: How dare you! You could have told me about that guy in New York!\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Oh, please. Could you put the toilet seat down after using it? Would that be asking too much?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I would have, but I knew you wouldn't put it back up ... </br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What is wrong with you two? Can't you see you are great together? Can't you ... see ... Why are you smiling?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Oh! Hi, Vanessa.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Eavesdrop much V?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You guys!", "id": 3, "time": "93300"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about beliefs, opinions, relationships or character traits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express annoyance about an action or an event in the present and in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express willingness and intention.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Is it ok for parents to spy or eavesdrop on their kids? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Is it ok for the government to eavesdrop on its citizens in order to keep them safe? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "I think someone is listening!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I don't like the <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">crass</span> manner in which your friends speak.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> \u201cCrass\u201d</span> means to be